(Information Security Policy) Tj T*
(Northwind Analytics | Document ISP-001 | Version 7.1 | Approved 14 January 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Purpose and scope) Tj T*
(This policy defines how Northwind Analytics protects the confidentiality, integrity and) Tj T*
(availability of its information assets. It applies to all employees, contractors, interns) Tj T*
(and) Tj T*
(third parties who access company systems or data, on any device, in any location.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Data classification) Tj T*
(All information must be classified into one of four levels. Public: approved for release) Tj T*
(outside) Tj T*
(the company. Internal: default for day-to-day business information; not for external) Tj T*
(release.) Tj T*
(Confidential: commercially sensitive information, including contracts, financial forecasts) Tj T*
(and) Tj T*
(unreleased product plans. Restricted: personal data, authentication secrets, security) Tj T*
(findings and) Tj T*
(anything whose disclosure would cause severe harm. Restricted data may only be processed on) Tj T*
(managed) Tj T*
(devices and may never be copied to personal storage or unapproved cloud services.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Access control) Tj T*
(Access is granted on the principle of least privilege and must be approved by the data) Tj T*
(owner.) Tj T*
(All accounts require multi-factor authentication. Passwords must be at least 14 characters,) Tj T*
(generated by the company password manager, and unique to each system. Shared accounts are) Tj T*
(prohibited. Access rights are reviewed quarterly, and are revoked within 24 hours of an) Tj T*
(employee) Tj T*
(leaving or changing role.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Device security) Tj T*
(Company laptops and phones must have full-disk encryption enabled, an automatic screen lock) Tj T*
(after) Tj T*
(10 minutes of inactivity, and the managed endpoint agent installed and running. Operating) Tj T*
(system) Tj T*
(and browser updates must be applied within 14 days of release, and within 48 hours where the) Tj T*
(update fixes a vulnerability rated critical. Personal devices may access company email and) Tj T*
(chat) Tj T*
(only through the managed application container.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Acceptable use) Tj T*
(Company systems are provided for business use. Incidental personal use is permitted where it) Tj T*
(does) Tj T*
(not interfere with work, incur cost, or introduce risk. Staff must not disable security) Tj T*
(controls,) Tj T*
(connect unapproved devices to the corporate network, install unlicensed software, or use) Tj T*
(generative) Tj T*
